#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# constant_array

#% text
# `constant_array(c, n)` gives a list of `n` copies of `c`; `constant_array(c, [n1, n2, ...])` gives nested lists of those dimensions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
constant_array(0, 4)
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0, 0]

#% cell
constant_array(x, [2, 3])
#% output
#= [[x, x, x], [x, x, x]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A zero matrix to fill in:

#% cell
dimensions(constant_array(0.0, [3, 3]))
#% output
#= [3, 3]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `table`, `pad_right`, `identity_matrix`
